# BSC Lab technique-level evidence assessments (ADR 0027 migration).
#
# Migrated 2026-07-13 per the ADR 0027 migration ledger
# (docs/ontology/ADR_0027_MIGRATION_LEDGER.md). Each retained legacy claim is
# superseded by an immutable sstim:EvidenceAssessmentClaim revision with an
# atomic bounded proposition, explicit scope, and qualified evidence basis;
# the three universal refutations are retired into scoped, dated
# KnowledgeStatusAssertions. Legacy IRIs remain as deprecated tombstones.
#
# Migration honesty (ledger rules): tier and direction are carried forward
# from the legacy editorial rating as the initial migration assessment under
# method/adr-0027-migration/1, pending re-assessment under a dedicated
# rubric. No historical review activity, search, or independence is invented;
# consequently no EvidenceReviewDecision exists yet and the derived workflow
# summary for these revisions is "provisional".
#
# Outcome, population, comparator, and intervention descriptors minted here
# are implementation-scoped named individuals, not SKOS concepts
# (ADR 0027 implementation clarifications; CLAUDE.md §5.1).

@prefix bsclab-evidence: <https://w3id.org/sstim/implementation/bsclab/evidence/> .
@prefix dct:   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix owl:   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sstim: <https://w3id.org/sstim#> .
@prefix sstim-ex: <https://w3id.org/sstim/exposure#> .
@prefix sstim-ref: <https://w3id.org/sstim/ref/> .
@prefix sstim-v: <https://w3id.org/sstim/vocab#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix prov:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix bsc-fw-tech: <https://w3id.org/sstim/framework/bsc/technique/> .

